id: ops-mqdi
title: "Guarded merge-driver launcher: omit-dev clone installs complete instead of failing on the devDependency import"
description: "The canonical consumer launcher statically imports pm-ops/merge-driver, but pm-ops is a devDependency. npm install --omit=dev with scripts enabled (a source checkout) fails with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND in prepare before any fallback runs. Raised by CodeRabbit on pm-web#156 and Greptile on pm-slack-standup#89 and pm-changelog#207; hub item pm-cli-website-xy19."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: fleet,launcher,merge-driver,omit-dev
created_at: "2026-09-22T20:52:55.599Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T18:47:01.794Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T18:46:57.798Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T18:46:57.798Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts ships in the package and imports only node builtins; pm-ops/merge-driver/prepare is an exported entry; fixture tests run the shipped template for: pm-ops absent (exit 0, exactly one notice), current (runs pm merge install), failing pm (status propagated), stale pm-ops without the export and pm-ops with a missing entry file (both fail loudly); release:check exits 0 with 100/100/100/100 coverage"
repro_steps: "Install a fresh package clone with npm ci --omit=dev so the development-only launcher dependency is absent. Current source evidence: merge-driver-prepare.ts, templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts, test/coverage-gate.test.ts."
resolution: "Reverified main eba7d5262fd7 (unchanged since audit): [PR #119](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/119) ships the builtin-only guarded prepare template and exported runtime delegate with absent/broken/working install tests. Retained evidence: merge-driver-prepare.ts, templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts, test/coverage-gate.test.ts."
expected_result: The builtin-only guarded prepare launcher permits omitted development dependencies and preserves errors for broken present installations.
